            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method for detecting a primary magnetic source, comprising generating a driving magnetic field above a threshold amplitude level wherein the primary magnetic source becomes non-linear, and detecting a response magnetic field comprising a first response component at a first frequency and a second response component at a second frequency. Primary portions of the first response component and the second response component are generated by the primary magnetic source, that has a non-linear response to the driving signal. Secondary portions of the first response component and the second response component are generated by a secondary magnetic source. The method comprises determining a driving factor representing a ratio of the first driving component and the second driving component in the driving signal, determining a correction factor corresponding to the secondary portion of the second response component, determining a detection signal corresponding to the primary portion of the second response component, and generating an output signal based on the detection signal.</p>
            </abstract>
